<s-1 id="RM000002245000X_01_0001" proc-id="E0505_____000000700000">
<ptxt>Handling of FIPG (Formed In Place Gasket)</ptxt>
<content1 releasenbr="1">
<atten3>
<ptxt>When removing the gasket, be careful not to let pieces of gasket enter the engine.</ptxt>
</atten3>
<s2>
<ptxt>Before applying seal packing, thoroughly remove any old seal packing from the sealing surfaces, bolts and bolt holes, and clean the sealing surfaces with white gasoline and brake cleaner.</ptxt>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>Using a shop rag, clean the contact surfaces of each part and its mating part so that they are free of oil, water and dirt. </ptxt>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>Apply FIPG to the part being installed.</ptxt>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>Apply to the specified width with neither too much nor too little, and always overlap the start and end of the application.</ptxt>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>After assembly, be careful not to move the parts.</ptxt>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>Install the parts within 3 minutes of applying.</ptxt>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>Do not add coolant, fill oil or start the engine until the specified time has elapsed after assembly.</ptxt>
</s2>
</content1>
</s-1>
